ANSWERS = [
    "Runlevel 3, from the <code>id:3:initdefault:</code> record in <code>/etc/inittab</code>. The second field is the runlevel; <code>grep initdefault /etc/inittab</code> finds it.",
    "<code>sudo systemctl isolate multi-user.target</code>. It stops every unit the new target doesn't need, including the graphical session and display manager.",
    "<code>systemctl list-unit-files --type=service --state=enabled --no-pager</code>. Units marked static start only when another unit pulls them in.",
    "systemd still has the old copy in memory. Run <code>sudo systemctl daemon-reload</code>, then restart the service, and check it with <code>systemctl cat NAME</code>.",
    "<code>sudo shutdown -r +15 'app02 reboots in 15 minutes, save your work'</code> warns logged-in users and schedules it. <code>sudo shutdown -c</code> cancels it.",
    "Package files under <code>/usr/lib/systemd/system</code> are replaced on updates. Put changes in <code>/etc/systemd/system</code>, ideally as a drop-in made with <code>sudo systemctl edit NAME</code>, then <code>daemon-reload</code>.",
    "acpid handles ACPI events such as the power button. Check it with <code>systemctl list-unit-files | grep acpid</code> or <code>systemctl status acpid</code>, and install it with <code>sudo apt install acpid</code> if missing.",
]
